%description:

Tcp.mss:auto-ipv4 -- with -1, an IPv4 host announces the MSS of an MTU of 1500 bytes.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "-1: the MSS of the address family for an MTU of 1500 bytes, 1460 for
IPv4 and 1440 for IPv6, when the peer is known".

The classes: auto (-1, the default), with a facet for IPv4 and one for IPv6; explicit (88 and
more); invalid (0 to 87, and below -1). The code: TcpConnection::initConnection() and
resolveAddressFamilyMss(). This test separates "auto" from "explicit".

Host under test: host1, the active opener, on IPv4. Observation: level 1, the MSS option of
the SYN of host1 is 1460.

%# parameter: Tcp.mss
%# class: auto-ipv4
%# value: -1
%# key: *.host1.tcp.mss
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMssAutoIpv4")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpMssOptionOf(context.event.packet) == 1460; })
                  .describe("the SYN of host1, with the MSS 1460")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMssAutoIpv4 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.mss = -1    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMssAutoIpv4: PASS
